    "content": "fuzzing/meson.build:17:# Links in a static library provided by oss-fuzz, else a standalone driver.\nfuzzing/meson.build:18:# https://github.com/google/oss-fuzz/blob/master/docs/new_project_guide.md#buildsh-script-environment\nfuzzing/fuzz.h:15:/* Disables logging for oss-fuzz. Must be used with each target. */\nfuzzing/README.md:1:Fuzz targets used by [oss-fuzz](https://github.com/google/oss-fuzz/).\nfuzzing/README.md:3:Useful links: [Dashboard](https://oss-fuzz.com/) _(requires access)_, [Build logs](https://oss-fuzz-build-logs.storage.googleapis.com/index.html), [Coverage](https://oss-fuzz.com/coverage-report/job/libfuzzer_asan_glib/latest)\nfuzzing/README.md:9:New targets are picked up by oss-fuzz automatically within a day. Targets must not be renamed once added.\nfuzzing/README.md:23:## How to reproduce oss-fuzz bugs locally\nfuzzing/README.md:43:If need be, [you can still reproduce](https://github.com/google/oss-fuzz/blob/master/docs/reproducing.md#building-using-docker) those bugs with the oss-fuzz provided docker images.\n> When authority is not present, the path cannot begin with two slash\n> characters (\"//\").\n\nThis is already encoded in an assertion at the top of\n`g_uri_join_internal()`.\n\nThe approach of prefixing the path with `/.` should be harmless: it\n--\nThis will make converting the docs to another format\n(say, rst) somewhat easier.\n\n0be6aa1b22d697bafe1991dcf47273cfcb5053be Merge branch 'reuse-fuzzing' into 'main'\nfuzzing: Add copyright/licensing headers to fuzzing files\n\nSee merge request GNOME/glib!2666\ne66277943d0e54edb2ab1029d0bb325e444de9e9 fuzzing: Add copyright/licensing headers to fuzzing files\nThe files have only been touched by a subset of three people: pdknsk,\nPhilip Withnall, and Marc-André Lureau. Their copyrights are assigned to\npdknsk, Endless OS Foundation and Red Hat.\n--\nstill is) LGPL-2.1-or-later.\n\n`driver.c` came from LLVM and is under a different license:\nhttps://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/blob/main/compiler-rt/lib/fuzzer/standalone/StandaloneFuzzTargetMain.c.\nThat doesn’t affect the license of GLib overall, since it’s only used\nfor testing during development.\n\n--\n\n70ee43f1e9695b78908e10f7619998052ce62611 glib: Add SPDX license headers automatically\nAdd SPDX license (but not copyright) headers to all files which follow a\ncertain pattern in their existing non-machine-readable header comment.\n\nThis commit was entirely generated using the command:\n```\n--\n5221b6a2612697751fd86467b0fbe7abc70b601d guri: Mark g_uri_get_host as nullable\nIt's currently annotated as not nullable, but it can be NULL.\n\n486a2cadbb22a6d9cbb3620e67f9dc0381a22b02 fuzzing: Add more GUriFlags to the URI parsing test\nWiden the amount of test coverage.\n\nSigned-off-by: Philip Withnall <pwithnall@endlessos.org>\n--\n\nHandle them more explicitly.\n\noss-fuzz#26083\n\nSigned-off-by: Philip Withnall <pwithnall@endlessos.org>\n\n--\n\nHandle them more explicitly.\n\noss-fuzz#26083\n\nSigned-off-by: Philip Withnall <pwithnall@endlessos.org>\n\nb43fb9cbfb033132e970f8b587d709c582dee1a0 guri: Fix URI scope parsing\nThe previous parsing code could read off the end of a URI if it had an\nincorrect %-escaped character in.\n\nFix that, and more closely implement parsing for the syntax defined in\n--\nThis requires reworking some network-address tests, which were\npreviously treating zone IDs incorrectly.\n\noss-fuzz#23816\n\nSigned-off-by: Philip Withnall <pwithnall@endlessos.org>\n\n7e400a886e4dd809f002941acb43ff3ba870b6aa guri: Refactor error handling in parse_ip_literal()\nHaving the goto labels at the bottom of a function makes things a little\nmore readable. This introduces no functional changes.\n\nSigned-off-by: Philip Withnall <pwithnall@endlessos.org>\n\n--\nFixes: #2149\n\n943b1e45ab3134e9028f7eb3c89b13de84f7ebf4 guri: Don’t fail g_uri_is_valid() if URI is missing a hostname\nAccording to my reading of\nhttps://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc3986#section-4, the only requirement for\na URI to be ‘absolute’ (actually, not a relative reference) is for the\nscheme to be specified. A hostname doesn’t have to be specified: see any\n--\nSigned-off-by: Philip Withnall <withnall@endlessm.com>\n\nb5c59cc3fc030080acc16c7f54e03cdb3e85a052 guri: Use gssize for array/string lengths\nThis reduces the possibility for overflow, and makes the code a little\nmore conventional to read.\n\nSigned-off-by: Philip Withnall <withnall@endlessm.com>\n\ne446c3487b6027203fbebcdfdd6dd8564bfbd5f7 guri: Change type of g_uri_escape_bytes() to use guint8\n`guint8` is the conventional way in modern GLib APIs to represent ‘a byte\nwhich could contain arbitrary binary’. `guchar` is not advised for that\n(even though it’s equivalent) because it could be misread as `gchar`.\n\nSigned-off-by: Philip Withnall <withnall@endlessm.com>\n\n--\n\n83597b9e579b3e3b5d897be32b8e3b18720b74c3 guri: Use NONE values of flags rather than 0\nThis introduces no functional changes, but makes the code a little\neasier to read.\n\nSigned-off-by: Philip Withnall <withnall@endlessm.com>\n\n--\n\n40873f845227a4a127657c6524b7e497fa5ab4d2 guri: Use g_steal_pointer() to make ownership transfer clearer\nThis introduces no functional changes, just makes the code a bit easier\nto read.\n\nSigned-off-by: Philip Withnall <withnall@endlessm.com>\n\n--\n\nSigned-off-by: Marc-André Lureau <marcandre.lureau@redhat.com>\n\n15bf2ddaf5cfae484f714ebb9f0895a79959f29e Merge branch 'ossfuzz-23815-23818-uri-overflows' into 'master'\nFix buffer read overflows in GUri\n\nSee merge request GNOME/glib!1559\nf9d165add1342ecae6cdde1b95e9ce63320768dd guri: Fix buffer overrun when decoding %-encoded URI components\nThere is a limited (1 or 2 byte) read off the end of the buffer if its\nfinal or penultimate byte is `%` and it’s not nul-terminated after that.\nIf the buffer *is* nul-terminated then the first `g_ascii_isxdigit()`\ncall safely returns `FALSE` and the code moves on.\n--\nstrings. See https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libsoup/-/merge_requests/126\nfor the fix there.\n\noss-fuzz#23815\noss-fuzz#23818\n\nSigned-off-by: Philip Withnall <withnall@endlessm.com>\n\n--\nRemove c-format from the string that is not c-formatted\n\nSee merge request GNOME/glib!1555\n39f8aff8f5158f24fa6a47cd8655a49eb4d72c7d fuzzing: Test URI parsing with and without the strict flag\nThis should test a few more code paths.\n\nSigned-off-by: Philip Withnall <withnall@endlessm.com>\n\n0bf12c8bfa201c01c40e03cb35195b7809284578 fuzzing: Use nul-terminated array introduced in previous commit\nThis fixes commit b2a6a9a434b29a70807dc9f811056318ff490bfa. Doh.\n\nSigned-off-by: Philip Withnall <withnall@endlessm.com>\n\n4fe91b63a3d3547421e0ddf1ef7c6aa6aca6a23c Remove c-format from the string that is not c-formatted\n\nb2a6a9a434b29a70807dc9f811056318ff490bfa fuzzing: Ensure input to g_uri_parse() is nul-terminated\nThe fuzzer will produce arbitrary binary blobs, which might not be\nnul-terminated. `g_uri_parse()` has no length argument, so relies on\nreceiving a nul-terminated string as input. Guarantee that.\n\nThis should fix fuzzing build failures like\nhttps://bugs.chromium.org/p/oss-fuzz/issues/detail?id=23750.\n\nSigned-off-by: Philip Withnall <withnall@endlessm.com>\n\ndd11160f7fecb6fcda89b61afd76700a54bfe0a7 fuzzing: Add fuzz tests for GUri parsing and escaping\nSigned-off-by: Philip Withnall <withnall@endlessm.com>\n\nHelps: #110",
